  "implementation_policy": "Distributed, massive helical extension spring reduced to 28 axial turn segments (open coils: small-helix-angle torsion theory E -> G -> k; closed coils: initial tension and coil contact; internal segment damping), a guided rigid carriage with its pan, and a freely falling 100 g calibration weight; passive unilateral pad contact with compression-only damping; fixed-step RK4 at 1/48000 s in Numba on the CPU (physics/simulate_spring.py, parameters in physics/scene.py, edits in edit_vocab.py). The state vector is cached at 24 Hz: video frame i is the native state at t=(i-1)/24 s. The timed edit restores the complete state vector of the accepted source cache at its frame and integrates on with the edited parameters. Blender 4.3.2 Cycles replays the caches (appearance/render_spring.py, base look); the render entry (by default) and the published suite use the appearance/realism.py overlay on it, 128 samples. Contact and damping values are effective parameters, not a calibrated instrument. tools/export_ground_truth.py writes pcve_ground_truth/1 from the caches.",
